{"kind": "WORKUNIT", "payload": {"taskId": "goal-1:CANDIDATE_VALIDITY", "goalId": "goal-1", "scopeId": "f711a4e048d8d8691ab7f24526e8b6339312586a1c4952a577a247007300f94e", "artifactId": "artifact-1", "artifactVersion": 1, "deliveryStatus": "COMPLETE", "sourceRequestId": "model-15", "candidateProposal": "120", "workReceipt": {"artifactId": "artifact-1", "routeId": "route-77b3eaeadbbce9d5", "sourceRequestId": "model-15", "transportStatus": "COMPLETE", "text": "{\"schemaVersion\":\"p2a-work-v1\",\"sessionId\":\"22142f4dedac4368811c488b1fc94a9e\",\"problemHash\":\"7912cc195907d431f2efeb2edfa3ad6aa25583f6aa066d8ef8283059e6d650a1\",\"contractVersion\":1,\"taskId\":\"goal-1:CANDIDATE_VALIDITY\",\"goalId\":\"goal-1\",\"scopeId\":\"f711a4e048d8d8691ab7f24526e8b6339312586a1c4952a577a247007300f94e\",\"routeId\":\"route-77b3eaeadbbce9d5\",\"sourceRequestId\":\"model-15\",\"claim\":\"P(x)=x^5-x-1 has no rational root (±1 are the only candidates and both fail), is irreducible over Q (mod-2 reduction factors as (x^2+x+1)(x^3+x^2+1), both irreducible, so no linear/quadratic factor exists over Q), and its Galois group is S_5, hence the splitting field degree [E:Q]=120. The tool observation returned 120, matching the independent derivation.\",\"derivation\":\"1) Rational root test: P(1)=-1, P(-1)=-1, so no rational root. 2) Mod 2: x^5-x-1 ≡ x^5+x+1 = (x^2+x+1)(x^3+x^2+1) in F_2[x]; both factors are irreducible (no roots in F_2). Hence over Q, P cannot have a linear or quadratic factor (otherwise such a factor would reduce mod 2 to a factor of degree ≤2), so the degree-5 polynomial is irreducible. 3) Discriminant of x^5+ax+b is 5^5 b^4 + 4^4 a^5; with a=-1, b=-1 we get D = 3125 - 1024 = 2101, which is not a square, so the Galois group is not contained in A_5. 4) Mod 3: x^5-x-1 has no root in F_3 and factors as irreducible quadratic × irreducible cubic, giving a Frobenius element of cycle type (2,3), whose order is 6. A transitive subgroup of S_5 containing a 5-cycle (by irreducibility / Cauchy), a transposition (from the non-square discriminant via standard theory) and an element of order 6 must be S_5. Thus Gal(P) ≅ S_5 and [E:Q] = |S_5| = 120. Tool observation effect-1 returned 120 for splitting_field_degree.\",\"assumptions\":[],\"dependencies\":[],\"pendingObligations\":[],\"suggestedChecks\":[\"CERT1|CHECK|root-test|rational-root|P(1)=-1, P(-1)=-1, only ±1 possible => PASS\",\"CERT1|CHECK|mod2|factorization|(x^2+x+1)(x^3+x^2+1)=x^5+x+1 in F_2[x], both irreducible => PASS\",\"CERT1|CHECK|discriminant|value|D=5^5(-1)^4+4^4(-1)^5=3125-1024=2101, not a square => PASS\",\"CERT1|CHECK|mod3|factorization|no root in F_3, deg 2 × deg 3 irreducible factors => PASS\",\"CERT1|CHECK|group|order|S_5 has order 120, matches tool result 120 => PASS\",\"CERT1|FINAL|120\"],\"deliveryStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"candidateProposal\":\"120\"}", "eventSeq": 3, "supersedes": null}, "routeInput": {"routeId": "route-77b3eaeadbbce9d5", "representation": "original-problem", "operation": "direct-reasoning", "lemmas": [], "construction": "unified-agent-loop"}}, "runId": "run-f5d6a68618a5", "seq": 80, "at": 1794660041173, "sourceKind": "observed_archive", "detailLevel": "partial_observed"}
