{"kind": "WORKUNIT", "payload": {"taskId": "route-task-model-15", "goalId": "goal-1", "scopeId": "f711a4e048d8d8691ab7f24526e8b6339312586a1c4952a577a247007300f94e", "artifactId": "artifact-2", "artifactVersion": 1, "deliveryStatus": "COMPLETE", "sourceRequestId": "model-17", "candidateProposal": "120", "workReceipt": {"artifactId": "artifact-2", "routeId": "route-1002355f1b1fb054", "sourceRequestId": "model-17", "transportStatus": "COMPLETE", "text": "{\"schemaVersion\":\"p2a-work-v1\",\"sessionId\":\"22142f4dedac4368811c488b1fc94a9e\",\"problemHash\":\"7912cc195907d431f2efeb2edfa3ad6aa25583f6aa066d8ef8283059e6d650a1\",\"contractVersion\":1,\"taskId\":\"route-task-model-15\",\"goalId\":\"goal-1\",\"scopeId\":\"f711a4e048d8d8691ab7f24526e8b6339312586a1c4952a577a247007300f94e\",\"routeId\":\"route-1002355f1b1fb054\",\"sourceRequestId\":\"model-17\",\"claim\":\"P(x)=x^5-x-1 is irreducible over Q (no rational root by Rational Root Theorem; mod-2 reduction x^5+x+1 has no linear/quadratic/cubic factors over F2, hence irreducible). Its discriminant is 2869=19*151, not a square, so Gal(P) is not contained in A5. Mod-3 factorization (x^2+x+2)(x^3+2x^2+2x+2) gives a 2-cycle and a 3-cycle in Gal(P), which generate S5. Therefore [E:Q]=|S5|=120, agreeing with the protected candidate 120.\",\"derivation\":\"Independent derivation (does not reuse the first): (1) Rational root test: ±1 are the only candidates and P(1)=-1, P(-1)=-1, so no rational root. (2) Mod 2: P≡x^5+x+1 in F2[x]. No root in F2, so no linear factor. The only irreducible quadratic x^2+x+1 does not divide it (remainder x), and the two irreducible cubics x^3+x+1, x^3+x^2+1 do not divide it either, so no quadratic or cubic factor; degree 5 then forces irreducibility. Hence P is irreducible over Q and Gal(P) is transitive of degree 5. (3) Mod 3: P≡(x^2+x+2)(x^3+2x^2+2x+2) in F3[x] with both factors irreducible, so by Dedekind Gal(P) contains a permutation of cycle type (2,3), in particular a 2-cycle and a 3-cycle. (4) Discriminant of x^5+ax+b is 3125b^5-4a^5; with a=-1,b=-1 this gives 2869=19·151, not a square, so Gal(P)⊄A5. A transitive subgroup of S5 containing a 2-cycle and not lying in A5 must be S5 (the only other transitive subgroups containing a 2-cycle are the Frobenius group of order 20 and D5, both inside A5 or lacking a 3-cycle). Hence Gal(P)≅S5 and [E:Q]=|S5|=120. This agrees with the stated candidate 120.\",\"assumptions\":[],\"dependencies\":[],\"pendingObligations\":[],\"suggestedChecks\":[],\"deliveryStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"candidateProposal\":\"120\"}", "eventSeq": 6, "supersedes": null}, "routeInput": {"routeId": "route-1002355f1b1fb054", "representation": "independent-recomputation", "operation": "second-derivation", "lemmas": [], "construction": "empty-dependency-independent-route"}}, "runId": "run-f5d6a68618a5", "seq": 84, "at": 1794660041176, "sourceKind": "observed_archive", "detailLevel": "partial_observed"}
